{{Administrative levels and divisions of Sinchew sidebar}}

The '''provinces of Sinchew''' are the first-level administrative divisions of the country. Sixteen were constituted in 1736 under the [[Constitution of Sinchew]] of 1733, and the number has changed with the annexation of [[Palpoa Province|Palpoa]], which was added in the nineteenth century.

New provinces were created in 1826 by the [[Provincial Restructuring Act]], which constituted further provinces by division from those already existing. The provinces of the republic are substantially the same units as those constituted in 1736, with the later provinces formed out of them.

Each province has an assembly of its own and elects two members of the [[Senate of Sinchew]] under the arrangement in force since 1736. The provinces of the west and centre hold about 31 per cent of the national territory and elect twenty-two of the thirty-two senators; the five provinces of the former [[Hachinawa]] hold about 69 per cent of the territory and elect ten.

== Provinces at present ==

The republic has twenty-three provinces. Thirteen are the provinces constituted in 1736, unchanged; nine were formed in 1826 by the division of three of them; and [[Palpoa Province|Palpoa]] was added in the nineteenth century.

