== Original Provinces (1736–1828) ==

The original provinces were constituted in 1736, three years after the constitution that provided for them.

The provinces described in this section are those created by the [[Provincial Restructuring Act]] of 1826, which retained the sixteen names and redrew the boundaries. The areas given are those of the modern provinces.

The boundaries were drawn by the Tianist minority in the constituent assembly. The class held about six per cent of the population in 1725 and most of the colony's capital, and it drew small provinces in the west and centre and large ones in the former Hachinawa. The eleven provinces of the west and centre average about 57,700 km² and hold about 57.9 per cent of the population; the five of the former empire average about 278,000 km² and hold about 42.1 per cent.

The provinces of the former Hachinawa are large because much of their territory was not under the republic's administration when the boundaries were drawn. The largest, [[Hashawa]], contains chiefdoms that had never been subject to the colony, and it was constituted as a single province rather than divided because its settled districts were few.

Each province bears a name in both of the Union's written languages. Names are rendered phonetically in the script that receives them and ordinary words semantically, so the two columns below are not translations of one another.

